# supabase/tests/targets.allow
#
# The ONLY Supabase projects `run.sh --target` may run against. One per line:
#
#   <20-letter project ref>   <name>
#
# NON-PRODUCTION PROJECTS ONLY. run.sh refuses to run at all if this file ever
# names the production project, and it refuses the production ref in a target
# URL whether or not this file mentions it.
#
# Adding a ref here is a decision, not a convenience: a target run writes inside
# transactions it rolls back, which still takes locks and fires triggers.

sbhlskvedpuxtneoaijw   aduatlas-staging
